The cw_odmr directory is for point measurements using the mfli lock-in amplifier + photodiode combo.
This is mostly just used for the Fraunhofer OLED-illumination samples.

The nv_setup directory is for point measurements using the single photon counting module (SPCM)
 + quantum machine. The Lorentzian_fit file which is used in nv_setup and in nv_widefield

nv_widefield directory is for widefield measurements using the PCO camera.
There is the main widefield_odmr
file which takes ODMR of each pixel independently, as well as many debug files which do some binning
or vary a certain parameter taking ODMRs at each point, etc. Most of the code here is copy-pasted
from one another with slight modifications, but where possible I call a pre-defined version of the
function, often in a helper class, to minimize the number of changes required when making modifications.
